<title>UK: SBC sets bond exchangeable into drug firms basket.</title>
<headline>SBC sets bond exchangeable into drug firms basket.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss Bank Corp (Jersey) has launched a $100-150 million notes issue which will be exchangeable into a basket of European life sciences stocks, sole manager SBC Warburg said.</p>
<p>The basket is made up of shares in Roche, Novartis, Glaxo Wellcome, SmithKline Beechham, and Zeneca. All have equal weighting.</p>
<p>The issue will be priced at a 19-21 percent conversion premium to the prevailing market level.</p>
<p> * * * * * * * * * *</p>
<p> AMT    $100-150 MLN  COUPON    *1.5-2.0     MATURITY  30.APR.01</p>
<p> TYPE   EXCHANGEABLE  PAY DATE   30.APR.97   YTM 3.125 - 3.625</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.50	ISS PRICE *94.125 - 94.625</p>
<p> MOODY	AA1	 LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA+	 DENOMS (K) ONE	 SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> NOTES     *INDICATED- PRICED LATER.</p>
<p>		HARD NON-CALL FOR TWO-YEARS THAN CALLABLE AT PAR.</p>
<p>		ISSUED UNDER AN MTN PROGRAMME.</p>
